        // Record state after second call
        uint256 ownerBalanceAfter2 = owner.balance;

        // The rule: If the first call succeeded (i.e., the call data was passed through as intended),
        // then the second call should also succeed (the buggy version sends empty data always,
        // potentially causing different behavior on the second call).
        // Specifically, the buggy version with empty data may revert on the second call if the target
        // address expects specific data, while the correct version passes through the data.
        // We assert that the success of both calls is the same when data is non-empty.
        // In the reference, both succeed; in the mutant, the second may fail because it always sends empty data.
